# graphify ignore rules for CopyClip
#
# Syntax note: these are fnmatch globs, NOT gitignore patterns. Each line is tested
# against the path relative to the scan root, the bare filename, and every individual
# path component, so a plain directory name like "otherCopyProjects" is enough and
# needs no trailing slash or wildcard.
#
# graphify already skips __pycache__, .git, build, dist, out, target, node_modules
# and venvs on its own, so those are deliberately not repeated here.

# The reason this file exists.
# otherCopyProjects holds 9 shallow clones of upstream projects (scrcpy, ClipCascade,
# Shizuku, kdeconnect-android and friends). Graphing them pushed the project to ~7,450
# nodes, past graphify's HTML visualisation limit, and the rebuild failed outright with
# "Graph has 7450 nodes - too large for HTML viz". They are reference material, not our
# code, so they have no business in this project's knowledge graph.
#
# Caveat: graphify has no negation syntax (no "!pattern"), so this blanket rule also
# excludes otherCopyProjects/NOTES.md. That is the deliberate trade: a rule that names
# the 9 clone directories individually would let NOTES.md through, but would silently
# break the graph again the moment clone_all.ps1 gains a tenth repo. Read NOTES.md
# directly; its conclusions are summarised in README.md anyway.
otherCopyProjects

# Build output. clipbridge.dex is generated from android/ClipBridge.java by
# android/build_dex.ps1; the Java source is the thing worth graphing.
bin
*.dex
*.class

# graphify's own output. Its built-in skip list contains "out" but not "graphify-out",
# so without this it re-ingests its own 63 KB GRAPH_REPORT.md and 227 KB graph.json on
# every run and the graph slowly eats itself.
graphify-out

# Runtime noise
logs
*.log

# Never graph the shared HMAC key
copyclip.key
*.key
